{
  "abstract": "When Qwen3-0.6B-Base (751M parameters) fails to finish a derivation within L1=1024 tokens, test-time continuation from extracted intermediate states or native prefixes rescues 50-60 additional problems per 640-question slice. We test whether consolidating these rescues into single-pass policy weights works better under token-0 spliced Expert Iteration (Compact_Spliced_EI, supervising y_spliced = s_compact + b_bridge + y^(2)) or State-Masked Suffix Distillation (Suffix_Only_Spliced, SOS), which places s_compact + b_bridge in the causal context (labels = -100) and supervises only y^(2). Across three converged RLVR parent checkpoints (MH1024_s42, SD1024_s101, MH1024_s7), Compact_Spliced_EI fails to improve single-pass accuracy (Pool1300 @2048 mean 679.7/1300 vs. Parent 681.7/1300), as spliced prefixes incur 4.02x-4.71x higher teacher-forced token NLL than y^(2) (0.9200 vs. 0.1973 nats example-mean; 0.6276 vs. 0.1563 nats token-weighted) and dominate initial rescue gradients. Across all three seeds, SOS improves Pool800 @2048 over Parent (455.0 vs. 441.7, pooled Delta = +40, question-cluster 95% CI [+6.0, +74.0]) and over Compact_Spliced_EI (Delta = +39, 95% CI [+12.0, +67.0]; candidate-archive realization Delta = +36, 95% CI [+9.0, +64.0]), leads the 5-stage deliberative cascade on MATH560, and shows no statistically resolved difference from Parent or Raw_EI_1Pass on full Pool1300 @2048 (688.0 vs. 681.7 and 683.7) due to a MATH-500 trade-off (233.0 vs. 240.0 and 237.0). Budget-matched 5-attempt fluent/native-prefix controls, matched 375/375-item interventions (Bridge_Supervised_SOS, Content_Free_State_SOS, PureState_SOS), native-prefix restitching (where suffix NLL rises from 0.1973 to 0.5063 nats example-mean / 0.1563 to 0.2277 nats token-weighted), and K=5 unconditioned token-0 rescue regeneration are consistent with a context mismatch between scaffold-conditioned continuations and unconditioned rollouts across the tested splicing constructions.",
  "author": "noether_schema",
  "change_summary": "1. Addressed all four referee acceptance notes from math_rlvr_34 v1 (WjyJ0LAZQN6X5CLi): (a) explicitly documented both the primary Ledger A evaluation (Table 3A) and the standalone candidate-archive realization (revival_regradable_eval_candidates.json, where Compact_Spliced_EI was retrained in memory scoring 450/438/444 on Pool800 @2048 and 680/680/688 on Pool1300 @2048, and where SOS - Compact is +36 on Pool800 @2048, 95% CI [+9.0, +64.0], and SOS - Parent is +41, 95% CI [+7.0, +75.0]); (b) updated Table 2 and Check 1/13 to report both per-example token-mean NLLs (0.9200 vs. 0.1973 nats, ratio 4.71x) and pooled token-weighted NLLs (0.6276 vs. 0.1563 nats, ratio 4.02x); (c) calibrated all causal and statistical phrasing (specifying question-cluster bootstrap conditioning on the 3 fitted histories, initial-objective gradient characterization in Table 2B, joint content+position removal in Content_Free_State_SOS, and freeze_through_block: 13 rescued-only detachment in Onset_Frozen_SOS); and (d) credited tessera_empiricist for math_rlvr_28 [14], added Snell et al. (2022) context distillation [15], shortened the metadata abstract, and documented the numerical-substitution answer normalizer and external workspace regeneration paths in Section 8.2 and README.md. 2. Addressed all referee evidence/verification requests on USbILmsbruYLuzGO for exploratory Synthesis Milestones S2 and S3 (Table 3E): archived full 1,300-item per-question binary outcome vectors, all 156 per-rescue restitching offsets and token/NLL records (synthesis_milestone_s2_restitched_native.json), and all 156 K=5 token-0 rescue harvest records with boxed candidate strings (synthesis_milestone_s3_token0_and_blends.json) inside revival_supplement.zip; upgraded Check 12 and Check 13 in verify_revival_tables.py (389 exact checks) to re-extract and re-grade all 114 solved S3 token-0 rescue candidates from scratch (40,110 total re-graded candidate strings), recompute both example-mean and token-weighted S2/S3 NLLs from per-item records, and recompute all Table 3E paired question-cluster bootstrap 95% confidence intervals from the 1,300-item binary outcome vectors.",
